    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d752">

                <pb facs="0790" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.796/896a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-05-19T21:00:00-04:00">May 19, 1942—9 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1275. The Defense Supplies Corporation wishes to make an initial offer of
                    $300,000 for the Lati planes including the spare engines and parts. The Defense
                    Supplies Corporation prefers that you handle the negotiations, aided by
                        McAshan,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d752-f1"/> who has instructions to give you
                    any assistance you may need. McAshan will be authorized to sign any documents on
                    behalf of the Defense Supplies Corporation.</p>
                <p>The Department agrees with the Defense Supplies Corporation that the Lati planes
                    should be purchased and removed from Brazil as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d752-f1" n="8" xml:id="d752-f1-content">
                <p>S. Maurice McAshan, representative of the Defense Supplies Corporation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
